// ============================================================================
// DAILY — 2026-10-01 (Thursday): Pure math sequence — Recamán's sequence
// ============================================================================
//
// THE SEQUENCE (OEIS A005132): a(0)=0; a(n) = a(n-1)-n if that value is
// POSITIVE and hasn't appeared yet in the sequence, else a(n-1)+n. A
// self-avoiding walk on the number line — forced to jump forward whenever
// stepping back would collide with a point it already visited.
// First 16 terms (a0..a15), the ones this piece plays:
//   0 1 3 6 2 7 13 20 12 21 11 22 10 23 9 24
// Taken mod 7 (one octave of a 7-note scale) for scale degrees:
//   0 1 3 6 2 0 6 6 5 0 4 1 3 2 2 3
// Repeated back-to-back degrees (the "6 6" and "2 2") are bumped an octave
// on the repeat (+7) rather than restated flat, same grace-note move
// 2026-09-17's Pascal's-triangle file used for its own repeats.
//
// THE DIRECTION BIT drives the filter: Recamán's own definition is binary at
// every step — subtract n (walk folding back toward where it's been) or add n
// (forced outward because subtracting would collide). Steps 1-15's directions:
//   + + + - + + + - + - + - + - +
// mapped straight onto the lead's cutoff: each '+' opens the filter ~150Hz,
// each '-' closes it ~300Hz, starting from 900Hz — the filter literally
// tracks whether the walk is pushing outward or folding back on itself.
//
// STRUCTURE: cycles 1-4 play the 16 terms forward, grouped 4-per-cycle, with
// a rest grid for breathing room. Cycles 5-8 are the EXACT RETROGRADE of
// cycles 1-4 — both the note order and the rest placement reversed, group by
// group — the walk retracing every one of its own steps, which is exactly
// what Recamán's sequence can never actually do (it's defined by refusing to
// revisit a value). The retrograde pass runs its cutoff pattern 1.4x
// brighter throughout: the retrace carries more momentum second time through.
//
// SCALE: E:mixolydian — a mode not yet used on a Thursday (Fibonacci: C minor
// pentatonic, Collatz: D harmonic minor, twin primes: E phrygian, Pascal's
// triangle: D dorian, Thue-Morse: A minor/aeolian).
//
// ARRANGEMENT — deliberately different from the last two Thursday slots.
// Thue-Morse (09-24) used a sawtooth lead + a DYAD sine drone (tonic+5th,
// echoing that sequence's two-symbol alphabet) with no drum layer. Pascal's
// triangle (09-17) used a square lead + triangle pad + one euclid(3,8) kick.
// Today's defining structure isn't two-symbol or row-summed, it's a walk
// relative to a SINGLE anchor point (0, which this 16-term stretch actually
// revisits three times — positions 0, 5, 9 — without ever retracing a step to
// get there) — so the drone here is a single sustained tonic, not a dyad, and
// the lead is triangle (crisp/piercing, MUSIC-KNOWLEDGE.md §1) against the
// sine drone's pure/soft tone, a different lead/drone timbre pairing from
// either prior Thursday. No percussion: a self-avoiding number walk has no
// inherent metric pulse to put a kit under, and the direction bits already
// have an audible outlet in the filter automation above — per
// MUSIC-QC-LOOP.md, a derived number needing an outlet doesn't by itself
// justify a drum kit as that outlet.
//
// TEMPO: setcpm(24), 4 quarter-note beats/cycle ≈ 96 BPM — a walking pace,
// fitting the topic. (Math-sequence day carries no genre-specific tempo
// mandate the way acid/techno slots do.)
// CYCLES: 8 (4 forward + 4 retrograde). setcpm(24) x 8 / 60 = 20s.
// ============================================================================

setcpm(24)

$lead: n(`<
  [0 ~ 1 3 ~ ~ 6 ~]
  [2 ~ ~ 0 6 ~ 13 ~]
  [5 ~ 0 ~ 4 1 ~ ~]
  [3 ~ 2 ~ 9 ~ 3 ~]
  [~ 3 ~ 9 ~ 2 ~ 3]
  [~ ~ 1 4 ~ 0 ~ 5]
  [~ 13 ~ 6 0 ~ ~ 2]
  [~ 6 ~ ~ 3 1 ~ 0]
>`)
  .scale("E:mixolydian")
  .sound("triangle")
  .attack(.01).decay(.08).sustain(.15).release(.12)
  .lpf(`<
    [900 1050 1200 1350]
    [1050 1200 1350 1500]
    [1200 1350 1050 1200]
    [900 1050 750 900]
    [1260 1050 1470 1260]
    [1680 1470 1890 1680]
    [2100 1890 1680 1470]
    [1890 1680 1470 1260]
  >`)
  .lpq(5)
  .gain(.4)
  .room(1)

$drone: n("0").scale("E:mixolydian")
  .sound("sine")
  .attack(2).release(3)
  .lpf(650)
  .gain(.2)
  .room(2)
